I normally use pico or nano on a unix machine. The other day, my linux guru
was helping me setup a RAID and the RH install didn't include pico, so he
had me using vim. I was turned off at first by the arbitrary letter
commands, but after using it a while, it seemed more useful for editing conf
files. For instance, with pico, I have typed an extra character somewhere in
a file while editing it, without noticing. Vi seems to prevent this with its
insert mode. That seems rather simple, but it was sort of like a sea change
for me.

You know, I think I'm finally starting to understand the NH philosophy. It
is a game in the Unix philosophy. Small, simple yet powerful, command line
oriented, open source. As a fortune says "Nethack is more than just a game".
Currently, it seems to me that NH is designed to make you a better unix
hacker. Think before you type!





